# {{.AppName}}

A Goose single-page application: a Go backend that serves JSON API routes
under `/api` and the built **{{.Framework}}** frontend for every other path
— one service, one port.

## Structure

```
{{.AppNameLower}}/
├── main.go            # Bootstraps the goose SPA platform (port 8080)
├── app/               # Backend modules (JSON API, routes served under /api)
├── frontend/          # {{.Framework}} source (builds into public/)
├── public/            # Built frontend assets (generated, git-ignored)
├── tests/             # Backend tests
└── Makefile           # install / dev / build / dist workflow
```

## Getting started

```bash
make install     # go mod tidy + npm install
make dev         # Go API on :8080 + {{.Framework}} dev server together
```

During development the {{.Framework}} dev server proxies `/api` requests to
the Go backend, so the frontend gets hot reload while hitting real endpoints.

## Routes

Backend routes are declared without the `/api` prefix — the platform adds it:

| Declared      | Served at          |
|---------------|--------------------|
| `GET /`       | `GET /api`         |
| `GET /version`| `GET /api/version` |

Any non-`/api` path serves a file from `public/` if it exists, and falls
back to `public/index.html` for client-side routes.

## Production

```bash
make dist        # frontend build -> public/, then binary + assets -> dist/
cd dist && ./{{.AppNameLower}}
```

## Make targets

| Target           | What it does                                        |
|------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| `install`        | Go + npm dependencies                               |
| `dev`            | Backend and frontend dev servers together           |
| `dev-backend`    | Go server only (:8080)                              |
| `dev-frontend`   | {{.Framework}} dev server only (`/api` proxied)     |
| `build-frontend` | Transpile/bundle frontend into `public/`            |
| `build`          | Compile the Go binary                               |
| `dist`           | Full distribution bundle in `dist/`                 |
| `run`            | Frontend build, then serve everything from Go       |
| `test`           | Go tests                                            |
| `clean`          | Remove binaries, builds, and installed dependencies |
